by the same surface (Dashboard). The RHOAI Pipelines team needs no separate validation epic because validation is exercised through the Dashboard comparison view itself. | — (AC on E001) |\n\nComponent name mappings: all epic `component` values (`Dashboard`,\n`Model Registry`, `Documentation`) are copied verbatim from\n`.context/rhai-components.txt`. No non-obvious mappings were needed.\nE001's scope spans the strategy components Dashboard and (passively)\nData Science Pipelines; the single most-relevant canonical name is\n`Dashboard`.\n\n## Investigation Epics (Step 3)\n\nNone. The strategy declares \"Open Questions: None\" and contains no risks\ntable, assumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. No unknown exists\nwhose resolution would change which epics exist or what they do.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view with side-by-side and diff modes in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Registered model version link back to producing run | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Documentation for the run comparison workflow | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n\nPriorities: E001 is P0 (enables HLR-1, the only P0 HLR). E002 is P1 (enables\nHLR-2, P1). E003 is P1 (enables the UI half of HLR-2; it inherits no P0\nbecause its prerequisites E001/E002 only gate P1 work through it). E004 is a\n`docs-authoring` epic: per the docs-authoring priority exception its priority\nis derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (its HLR-4 is\nP2, but docs epics do not inherit from HLRs and do not push priority\nupstream).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n  E001[\"E001 Dashboard comparison view (P0)\"] --> E003[\"E003 Registry entry point (P1)\"]\n  E002[\"E002 Registry run link-back (P1)\"] --> E003\n  E001 --> E004[\"E004 Documentation (P1)\"]\n  E002 --> E004\n  E003 --> E004\n```\n\nCritical path length: 3 (E001 → E003 → E004, and E002 → E003 → E004).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The registry entry point consumes the run comparison surface delivered by the Dashboard comparison view; it builds on that UI surface rather than recreating it. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The Dashboard registry entry point builds against the run-link metadata that the Model Registry exposes on registered model versions. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the implemented comparison workflow; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n| (no edge) E001 ↔ E002 | Rule 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Dashboard and Model Registry are different components in different repos with no shared artifact; they run in parallel. |\n| (no edge) E001 ↔ E004 priority coupling | docs-authoring priority exception | E004 is P1 by strategy priority, not by inheritance from E001; no P0 propagation. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|-------------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters and metrics side by side in the Dashboard. | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Core P0 capability; runs-list entry point. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. | RHAISTRAT-9015-E002, RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Splits across components per Rule 1: registry data model (E002, Model Registry team) and Dashboard registry-UI entry point (E003, RHOAI Dashboard team — the registry UI lives in the Dashboard per architecture context). |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs. | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 (bundled) | Consolidated with HLR-1, not split by priority: the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data (same component, same team, same view). The strategy itself notes requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. Splitting would produce two epics building the same UI surface plus an artificial serialization edge; E001 covers both HLR ids at the P0 priority. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry. | RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | `docs-authoring` epic, blocked by all Implementation epics; epic priority P1 via the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major), not via inheritance from P2. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies\n  table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no non-functional\n  requirements. Owner teams were inferred from the architecture context files\n  (`dashboard.md` → RHOAI Dashboard, `model-registry.md` → Model Registry).\n  The docs epic was assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard team as the owner of the\n  primary documented surface; confirm the docs owner during planning.\n- **Passive component treatment**: Data Science Pipelines is listed as\n  affected but the strategy states no code change for it. It is treated as\n  passive (run parameters/metrics are already surfaced on per-run pages per\n  the problem statement); validation is an acceptance criterion on E001. If\n  per-run parameter/metric surfacing for pipeline runs turns out to be\n  incomplete, DSP work would need to be added.\n- **Training-run source unspecified**: the strategy requires comparison of\n  \"training and pipeline runs\" but lists no training-workload component\n  (e.g. Training Operator) as affected. The problem statement says parameters\n  and metrics already live in per-run pages, so training-run data is assumed\n  already accessible to the Dashboard. If that assumption fails at\n  implementation time, it is a fix-and-retry on E001, not a decomposition\n  change (no open question was declared).\n- **Priority note (not an inversion)**: E004 is P1 while its only HLR (HLR-4)\n  is P2 — this is the mandated docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n  priority Major → P1), recorded here for reviewer visibility.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing and\nno dependency-gated work; E001 and E002 deliver independent value in parallel.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":21618,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94faa7bb4aaa1291","agent_id":"a049dec4cb7cb3d03","session_id":"3bd12ba6-3337-4052-a2c5-e0a73bbdce00","uuid":"3934495f-fbed-40ec-a0c3-bc64060301b8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:16:03.051Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
