{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-61331b10-09a4-4726-8ce4-6a16091bad1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57dced72deb442f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-8iih_m9g/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view with side-by-side and diff modes in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers a run comparison surface in the Dashboard: users select two or more\ntraining and pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by\nside, with a diff presentation that highlights which parameters and metrics\nchanged between two selected runs. This is the core user-facing capability of\nthe experiment-comparison strategy and the surface that the Model Registry\nentry point and the documentation build on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-select of runs (training and pipeline) from a project's runs list in\n  the Dashboard.\n- A comparison view that renders each selected run's parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- A diff presentation within the same comparison view that highlights which\n  parameters and metrics differ in value between two selected runs.\n- Comparison of runs of mixed kinds (training and pipeline) in the same view.\n- Comparison stays scoped to a single project; cross-project and\n  cross-cluster comparison is out of scope per the strategy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project's runs list, when the user selects two or more runs, a\n  comparison view opens showing each selected run's parameters and metrics\n  side by side.\n- Given two selected runs in the comparison view, the parameters and metrics\n  whose values differ between the two runs are visually highlighted.\n- Given completed Data Science Pipelines runs in the project, their\n  parameters and metrics are included and render correctly in the comparison\n  view (passive validation of Data Science Pipelines — no code change\n  expected there).\n- Given a selection mixing training runs and pipeline runs, both run kinds\n  render in the same comparison view.\n- All comparison interactions remain within a single project; no\n  cross-project or cross-cluster selection is offered.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can select two or more runs and view their parameters\n  and metrics side by side in the Dashboard.\n- HLR-3 (P1): provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which parameters and\n  metrics changed between two selected runs — consolidated with HLR-1 as a\n  presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data;\n  covered by this epic at its P0 priority.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30770,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94faa7bb4aaa1291","agent_id":"a049dec4cb7cb3d03","session_id":"3bd12ba6-3337-4052-a2c5-e0a73bbdce00","uuid":"44b5e29c-0b91-4239-be17-748e45461075","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:16:11.825Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
