{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-61331b10-09a4-4726-8ce4-6a16091bad1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-922aa2512fd6f74f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-8iih_m9g/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Registered model version link back to producing run\n\n## Description\n\nThe Model Registry records, on each registered model version, a link to the\nrun that produced it, and exposes that link through the registry's API so\nthat other surfaces (such as the Dashboard's registry UI) can resolve the\nsource run of a model version and open a comparison from it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Record the producing-run reference on registered model versions, using the\n  model version metadata extension point for structured custom properties.\n- Expose the run link through the registry's REST API so a consumer can\n  resolve the producing run of a given model version.\n- Keep existing registered model versions without a run link valid and\n  readable (backward compatible; no migration required).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered from a run, the registry records a link\n  identifying the run that produced it.\n- Given an API query for a model version that has a run link, the link is\n  returned in the response.\n- Given model versions registered before this change (no run link present),\n  those versions remain readable and valid through the API and UI.\n- The link representation is defined such that a Dashboard surface can\n  resolve the linked run within its project.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1, registry half): registered model versions link back to the run\n  that produced them.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30770,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94faa7bb4aaa1291",