tions: 1` is consistent with the declared\n73\t\"Open Questions: None\"; E004's `human_process_gates: -1` matches its mandatory\n74\ttechnical-review AC. `architecture_claims` calibration verified against\n75\t`.context`: dashboard.md (\"Single-pane web console... surfaces... pipelines...\n76\tComponent backends via Kubernetes CRs\") corroborates E001; model-registry.md\n77\t(\"Custom properties on model versions are the extension point\", \"REST API...\n78\tOpenAPI-specified\", \"Dashboard for the registry UI\") corroborates E002 and\n79\tE003. All cited files exist and support the stated premises.\n80\t\n81\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n82\t\n83\tEvery epic has testable Given/When/Then-style ACs derived from the strategy.\n84\tRule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E004 (docs-authoring) has the\n85\ttechnical-review-before-publication AC; E002, while additive rather than a\n86\treplacement, still carries a backward-compatibility AC for pre-existing model\n87\tversions. No konflux chain, so no build-pipeline AC is required. No misfiled\n88\tsoft ACs — E001's Data Science Pipelines AC conditions what the epic itself\n89\tverifies, and E004's review AC is part of the docs workflow deliverable. No\n90\tbare draft-ID (E00x) references in any epic body.\n91\t\n92\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n93\t\n94\tThe full strategy scope is covered: multi-select and side-by-side comparison,\n95\tdiff highlighting, mixed training/pipeline runs, single-project scoping (E001);\n96\trun link-back with backward compatibility (E002); registry entry point with\n97\tgraceful degradation (E003); documentation of both entry points plus\n98\tprerequisites and limits (E004). Out-of-scope items (auto promotion,\n99\tcross-project/cluster) are respected and explicitly documented as limits in\n100\tE001/E003/E004. Strategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: the\n101\tconsolidated-from-two-councils note appears in the matrix, and the missing\n102\tstrategy sections,